{"author":{"id":"a51b5961cc6de343a64125d8eb6a0f965aa434020b9c46ed932a1bbf143eb532"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1791724559,"nonce":"t/o9XlDzXOH4A0SPuLXwCamfsl8=","title":"Liquid glass draws the wrong image after the Images page","message":"Reported: moving from the Images page to Liquid glass, the lens's background showed other pictures from the image atlas. Reproduced at scale 2, headless: images then glass renders differently from glass alone.\n\nCause (1eaf09c's rectangular atlas): after the Images page the atlas was 2048x3584, stacked in a narrow column. The glass picture grew it to 4096 wide, still found no room, and threw full. The grow had replaced the texture, but the renderer cleared its bind groups only when add() returned, so after the reset it kept drawing through bind groups that named the destroyed texture.\n\nFix: the atlas grows only to a size where the entry fits, wider rather than taller than wide, so it never grows and then fails. The renderer also clears its bind groups whenever the atlas revision changed, even if add() throws.\n\nTest: native-images draws a 2000-square image, then a 2000x2048 one that makes the atlas widen. It checks the colour drawn. With the new growth rule a grow-then-fail cannot be produced, so no test reaches the old path; images then glass matches glass alone.","files":null}]}